From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: ntdll, kernelbase, winecfg, wine.inf: Windows 10 is 22H2 (build 19045)

Wine reported build 19043 (21H1, out of support since December 2022), and
programs that require 21H2 or later refuse to start -- Paint.NET 5: "Windows
10 (version 21H2), Windows 11, or newer is required". Windows 10's last
release is 22H2, build 19045: the version table, kernelbase's manifest
table, winecfg and the registry now say so, with DisplayVersion "22H2",
ReleaseId "2009" and an update revision (UBR). The registry values are
written without FLG_ADDREG_NOCLOBBER, so an existing prefix -- whose
CurrentBuildNumber is what ntdll reports when no version is configured --
moves on at its next `wineboot -u`.

Gate: test/winver-gate.sh.
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/version.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/version.c
@@ -168,7 +168,7 @@
     },
     /* WIN10 */
     {
-        sizeof(RTL_OSVERSIONINFOEXW), 10, 0, 19043, VER_PLATFORM_WIN32_NT,
+        sizeof(RTL_OSVERSIONINFOEXW), 10, 0, 19045, VER_PLATFORM_WIN32_NT,
         L"", 0, 0, VER_SUITE_SINGLEUSERTS, VER_NT_WORKSTATION, 0
     },
     /* WIN11 */
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/version.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/version.c
@@ -156,7 +156,7 @@
     },
     /* Windows 10 */
     {
-        { 10, 0, 19043 },
+        { 10, 0, 19045 },
         {0x8e0f7a12,0xbfb3,0x4fe8,{0xb9,0xa5,0x48,0xfd,0x50,0xa1,0x5a,0x9a}}
     }
 };
